.title Character Development Workshop
## 👥 Character Analysis

<?characters.main_character>
### Protagonist: <!characters.main_character.name>

**Archetype**: <!characters.main_character.archetype>
**Fatal Flaw**: <!characters.main_character.flaw>
**Deepest Desire**: <!characters.main_character.desire>
**Growth Arc**: <!characters.main_character.arc>

<?characters.main_character.backstory_complete bool>
✅ **Backstory Complete**: Well-developed background
</characters.main_character.backstory_complete>

<?characters.main_character.needs_development bool>
🔧 **Development Needed**: Character needs more depth in: <!characters.main_character.weak_areas>
</characters.main_character.needs_development>
</characters.main_character>

<?characters.antagonist>
### Antagonist: <!characters.antagonist.name>

**Type**: <!characters.antagonist.type>
**Motivation**: <!characters.antagonist.motivation>
**Methods**: <!characters.antagonist.methods>

<?characters.antagonist.sympathetic bool>
💡 **Sympathetic Villain**: Your antagonist has relatable motivations - this adds depth!
</characters.antagonist.sympathetic>

**Conflict Style**: <!characters.antagonist.conflict_style>
</characters.antagonist>

<?characters.supporting_cast int>
### Supporting Characters (<!characters.supporting_cast> total)

<?characters.supporting_cast gt 5>
⚠️ **Character Overload**: You have many supporting characters. Make sure each serves a unique purpose!
</characters.supporting_cast>

**Key Supporting Roles**:
- <!characters.support_1.name>: <!characters.support_1.role>
- <!characters.support_2.name>: <!characters.support_2.role>
- <!characters.support_3.name>: <!characters.support_3.role>
</characters.supporting_cast>

.title Plot Structure Analysis
## 📊 Story Structure

**Structure Type**: <!plot.structure_type>
**Current Act**: <!plot.current_act int>/<!plot.total_acts int>

### Plot Points Checklist:
<?plot.inciting_incident bool>
✅ **Inciting Incident**: Completed
</plot.inciting_incident>

<?plot.first_plot_point bool>
✅ **First Plot Point**: Completed  
</plot.first_plot_point>

<?plot.midpoint bool>
✅ **Midpoint**: Completed
</plot.midpoint>

<?plot.climax bool>
✅ **Climax**: Completed
</plot.climax>

<?plot.resolution bool>
✅ **Resolution**: Completed
</plot.resolution>

### Pacing Analysis
**Current Pace**: <!plot.pacing>
**Tension Level**: <!plot.tension_level int>/10

<?plot.tension_level lt 4>
📈 **Pacing Note**: Consider adding more conflict or stakes to increase tension.
</plot.tension_level>

<?plot.tension_level gt 8>
⚠️ **High Intensity**: Make sure to give readers breathing room between intense scenes.
</plot.tension_level>

